egal or agreed definition of old, so the words promise nothing on their own."]],"style":{"notes":["Loire wines tend to be fruity, with fresh, crisp flavors from high acidity, especially when young.","Many go through a dumb phase between two and five years, and the best can then age 20 years.","Sweetness runs from bone dry (sec) to very sweet moelleux wines, often touched by noble rot.","Sauvignon Blanc tastes of gooseberry and grapefruit, and cool years give lighter, more mineral wines.","Loire Pinot Noir is very light in body and color, and ripe Cabernet Franc smells of raspberry and pencil shavings."],"of":"Loire Valley"},"blurb":{"text":"A Loire Valley rosé appellation made from Cabernet Franc, Cabernet Sauvignon, Gamay, Grolleau, Pineau d'Aunis and Pinot Noir."},"study":true,"levels":[3],"sources":[{"name":"Candiago et al. 2022, A geospatial inventory of regulatory information for wine protected designations of origin in Europe, Scientific Data (product specifications as of 2021)","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-022-01513-0"},{"name":"INAO, the appellation's cahier des charges, chapter V (grapes and their shares), from the Bulletin officiel du ministère de l'Agriculture (Licence Ouverte)","url":"https://www.inao.gouv.fr/rechercher-un-produit"},{"name":"Fick and Hijmans 2017, WorldClim 2.1 monthly averages for 1970 to 2000, 2.5 minute grid (about 4.5 km)","url":"https://www.worldclim.org/data/worldclim21.html"},{"name":"Beck et al. 2023, High-resolution (1 km) Koppen-Geiger maps, Scientific Data (1991 to 2020)","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-023-02549-6"},{"name":"Winkler, Cook, Kliewer and Lider 1974, General Viticulture, University of California Press (heat summation regions)","url":null},{"name":"Jones 2010, Climate, grapes, and wine: structure and suitability in a variable and changing climate, VIII International Terroir Congress (which grapes suit which growing season temperatures)","url":"https://ives-openscience.eu/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/C